{"path":"io/c/remove","title":"std::remove","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>remove","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/c/remove","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Deletes the file identified by the character string pointed to by pathname.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstdio\">&lt;cstdio&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> remove<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> pathname <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Deletes the file identified by the character string pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pathname</span></code>.\n</p><p>If the file is currently open by any process, the behavior of this function is implementation-defined. POSIX systems unlink the file name (directory entry), but the filesystem space used by the file is not reclaimed while it is open in any process and while other hard links to the file exist. Windows does not allow the file to be deleted in such cases.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> pathname\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to a null-terminated string containing the path identifying the file to delete\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> upon success or non-zero value on error.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/remove.html\" data-external=\"1\">POSIX specifies</a> many additional details for the behavior of this function.\n</p><p>The standard library also defines a function template <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/remove\"><code>std::remove</code></a> taking a pair of iterators and a value, this overload is one of the standard <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm\">algorithms</a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdio&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdlib&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;fstream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// create a file, check success using operator! of temporary stream object</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ofstream\"><span class=\"kw1750\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ofstream</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"file1.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">put</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'a'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/perror\"><span class=\"kw1890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">perror</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Error creating file1.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/EXIT_status\"><span class=\"kw977\">EXIT_FAILURE</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ifstream\"><span class=\"kw1749\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ifstream</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"file1.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">rdbuf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// print file</span>\n&nbsp;\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">remove</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"file1.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// delete file</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ifstream\"><span class=\"kw1749\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ifstream</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"file1.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"co1\">// uses operator! of temporary stream object</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/perror\"><span class=\"kw1890\">std::<span class=\"me2\">perror</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Error opening deleted file\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/EXIT_status\"><span class=\"kw977\">EXIT_FAILURE</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/EXIT_status\"><span class=\"kw976\">EXIT_SUCCESS</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>a\nError opening deleted file: No such file or directory</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/remove\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>remove</span><span>remove_all</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  removes a file or empty directory<br>removes a file or directory and all its contents, recursively <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/rename\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>rename</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  renames a file <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/io/remove\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>remove</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/c","title":"C-style file input/output"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::remove","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Deletes the file identified by the character string pointed to by pathname."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"pathname"},{"label":"Return value","note":"0 upon success or non-zero value on error."},{"label":"Notes","note":"POSIX specifies many additional details for the behavior of this function."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"remove, remove_all","note":"removes a file or empty directoryremoves a file or directory and all its contents, recursively"},{"label":"rename","note":"renames a file"}]}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":253,"codeBlockCount":2}
